---
import LegalPage from '../components/legal/LegalPage.astro'
import { site } from '../lib/site'
---

<LegalPage
  title="Terms of service"
  description="The terms that apply when your organization uses Heftra: accounts, plans and billing, ownership of your data, AI output, liability and Danish law."
  lastUpdated="2026-10-06"
>
  <p>
    These terms apply when an organization ("you") uses Heftra. By signing an
    order or using the service, you agree to them on behalf of your
    organization.
  </p>

  <h2>The service</h2>
  <p>
    Heftra connects to your ERP, categorizes your spend, and gives you analysis
    such as cheaper alternatives, agreement compliance and spend-based emissions
    estimates. We may improve and change the service, and will not remove a core
    feature of your plan during a paid term without notice.
  </p>

  <h2>Accounts</h2>
  <p>
    You are responsible for the people you invite and for keeping sign-in
    details secure. Tell us promptly if you suspect unauthorised access.
  </p>

  <h2>Plans and billing</h2>
  <p>
    Fees follow your chosen plan and are billed monthly or yearly in advance,
    excluding VAT. Monthly plans can be cancelled with effect from the end of
    the month, yearly plans from the end of the year. Fees already paid are not
    refunded, except where the law requires it.
  </p>

  <h2>Your data</h2>
  <p>
    You own the data you bring into Heftra. We use it only to provide the
    service to you, as set out in our
    <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> and the data processing agreement.
    You can export your data while your subscription is active and for 30 days
    after it ends, after which it is deleted.
  </p>

  <h2>AI output</h2>
  <p>
    Heftra uses AI to categorize spend and to read agreements. Its output is
    decision support: it can be wrong, and you should review it before acting on
    it. Heftra flags uncertain results and never overwrites a correction made by
    your team.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    Do not use Heftra to break the law, to try to access other customers' data,
    to disrupt the service, or to resell it without our agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>Availability and support</h2>
  <p>
    We aim to keep Heftra available at all times and to tell you about planned
    maintenance in advance. Support is provided by email; the Enterprise plan
    includes priority support.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    Neither party is liable for indirect or consequential loss, including lost
    profits. Each party's total liability in a year is limited to the fees paid
    for the service in the twelve months before the claim. These limits do not
    apply where the law does not allow them.
  </p>

  <h2>Ending the agreement</h2>
  <p>
    Either party can end the agreement at the end of a billing period, or
    straight away if the other party seriously breaches these terms and does not
    fix it within 30 days of notice.
  </p>

  <h2>Law and disputes</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by Danish law, and disputes go to the Danish
    courts.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms:{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
